<title>USA: General Re sets $500 mln stock buyback.</title>
<headline>General Re sets $500 mln stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Re Corp, a reinsurance company, said Wednesday its board has authorized a new program to repurchase up to $500 million of its common stock, the 10th program under its buyback plan.</p>
<p>In the last program, it said General Re said it bought 1.185 million common shares from January 1, 1997 to April 8, 1997 for $192.5 million.</p>
<p>Since it started buying back its common shares in June 1987, the company has bought back 28,318,500 shares at a total cost of $2.53 billion, it said.</p>
